      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced SMALLEST_TYPE is needed. As I understand it, EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_REQ_ONLY should be used when the response size varies,  EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_RESP_ONLY should be used when the request size varies, and EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_UNBOUND should be used when both vary.\n\nFor handlers that support multiple versions the bounds for each version must be checked by that handler. The SMALLEST_TYPE check may even lead developers to assume the response size does not need to be checked in the handler.",
